# Drishti Workbench — configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and adjust if your model server runs somewhere other than the
# default. This file lists every variable the application reads.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There are NO API KEYS here, and there never will be.
#
# Drishti is air-gapped by design: it runs inside the plant network with no
# route to the internet. All model inference is served by a local engine. If
# you ever find yourself adding OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# GOOGLE_API_KEY or anything similar, stop — that is a design violation, not a
# missing feature. See the warning at the top of README.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the OpenAI-compatible model server, including the /v1 suffix.
#
# Points to Ollama for local Mac development/demo. For production deployment
# on MRPL's GPU server, this URL points to a vLLM instance instead — no other
# code changes required. Both engines speak the same /v1/chat/completions
# protocol, which is all the application depends on.
#
#   Ollama, running on your Mac:     http://localhost:11434/v1
#   Ollama, via docker compose:      http://ollama:11434/v1   (set for you)
#   vLLM, on MRPL's GPU server:      http://gpu-server.internal:8000/v1
MODEL_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Model used when a request does not name one. An Ollama tag here; on vLLM this
# becomes the served model name, e.g. Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct.
DEFAULT_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b
